rota lap 4489, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; every row had been read today, so the computed row stood. The fixed seat, context/TWO_ROOMS.md, sends a reader to the doorway guard, and that guard's own WHAT IS NOT PROVEN block is the sentence this lap followed.
think Earth reads the concrete fact at the door before the argument, so the lap started by RUNNING the doorway census rather than reasoning about it. It reads fails=3 at ceiling=3, all three dated testimony under active-designing/date/20260820/ -- the 44-to-48 regrowth the baton names was swept and is now walled by the commit-time touch scan. That reading closed a question rather than opening one.
think The card carries an open general form from Incense (20260909.204315): every scan carries a WHAT IS NOT PROVEN block and nothing walks that queue. Measured: git grep -l over tools/ answers 84 files, one block each. All 84 were read.
think Four markers counted with rerunnable greps, overlapping on purpose -- 47 decline a judgment, 13 wait on an absent machine (9 of them the one Caravan `no kernel booted`), 11 wait on a seat or a law page, 8 name a sibling guard that owns the question. So the heading carries at least five jobs and only the fifth is work anyone could take.
think The queue that is genuinely a queue names five, each in its guard's own words. The sharpest was checked at its source rather than taken from the block: tools/fixtures/f/foundations_link_scan.sh:19 strips an anchor and checks the path alone, and no guard in this tree resolves a `#heading` anywhere.
think Reds first, at the cold pass: tracked_link red was MINE -- construction/ITINERARY.md linked the shelf I had just written and never staged, so the guard read the tracked index and refused. Staged, GREEN.
think stash_record red was a whole finished Grass lap sitting in stash@{0} -- a foundation page, its foundations/README.md row, its session log, its shelf row, and an ITINERARY account shelf. Recovered the four durable artifacts byte for byte from stash@{0}^3 and the tracked hunk, re-ordered the shelf row into stamp order, and stash_record reads unlanded=0.
obs I DECLINED the recovered shelf on taste and a guard refused the decision, which is the lap's second finding. construction/archive/20260909-212542_itinerary-landed-accounts.md holds the SAME GRASS account, byte for byte, as the tracked 20260909-215853 shelf -- shelved twice thirty-three minutes apart because the first shelving never landed -- so landing it puts a duplicate immutable shelf in the tree, and I left it out.
obs log_file_claim then reddened at the hot pass: the recovered log names that shelf in a file field, and the guard reads a staged log's claims against tree and index. It cannot tell a later hand's lawful decline from a fabricated citation, and it is right not to try. Landing the shelf was the honest close -- the lap DID write it, the card DID carry that account before 21:25, and the cost is one orphans_shelf=1, which stash_record reports and never gates. A record is whole or it is edited, and editing another lap's log to fit my taste is the move a guard exists to refuse.
obs The stashed construction/ITINERARY.md stays declined: it is three laps stale and the live card carries the live account. Nothing cites it, so no guard objects -- which is the difference between the two declines.
obs One figure in the recovered foundation had gone stale in two hours: it read `10 of 12` where sh tools/c/convergence_census.sh now answers 10 proven of 13. Repaired to name the stamp and to say RUN rather than READ, since the denominator is free -- which is the page's own thesis turned on the page itself.
obs No new field is proposed for the 84 blocks. A class token would ask each future guard to classify its gap at the moment it is least able to, and the card already ranks work.
